\name{hapmapsnp6-package}
\alias{hapmapsnp6-package} \alias{hapmapsnp6}
\docType{package}
\title{
  Sample HapMap SNP 6.0
}
\description{

  Sample dataset on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, for the
  HapMap samples NA06985, NA06991 and NA06993. The package is meant to be
  used only for demonstration of Bioconductor tools.

  As of version 1.55.1 the data is no longer shipped inside the package. It
  is deposited on Zenodo, under \code{doi:10.5281/zenodo.23990454}, and
  served through \pkg{ExperimentHub}. The first call to an accessor
  downloads the resource and stores it in the local ExperimentHub cache;
  later calls read from that cache.

}
\section{Accessing the data}{

  Four resources are provided: the genotype calling result
  \code{crlmmResult}, a \code{SnpSet}, and the three CEL files it was
  derived from.

  \describe{
    \item{\code{\link{crlmmResult}()}}{Returns the \code{SnpSet}. This
      replaces \code{data(crlmmResult)}, used by earlier versions of the
      package, which no longer works because the package ships no data
      directory. With \code{metadata = TRUE} it returns the resource
      metadata without downloading the object.}
    \item{\code{\link{celFiles}()}}{Returns the paths of the three CEL files
      on disk, named after the original files.}
    \item{\code{\link{celFiles}(asDir = TRUE)}}{Returns a directory holding
      the three files. This replaces
      \code{system.file("celFiles", package = "hapmapsnp6")}, which cannot
      work for files that are no longer installed with the package.}
  }

}
\details{

  The origin of the data and the processing that produced
  \code{crlmmResult} are documented in \code{inst/scripts/make-data.R}. The
  resource records served through ExperimentHub are listed in
  \code{inst/extdata/metadata.csv}.

  The maintainer does not warrant the accuracy of the data.

}
\author{
  Data generated by the HapMap Consortium.

  Package maintained by Benilton Carvalho <benilton@unicamp.br>.
}
\references{
The International HapMap Consortium. The International HapMap
Project. Nature 426, 789-796 (2003).
}
\seealso{
  \code{\link{crlmmResult}}, \code{\link{celFiles}},
  \code{\link[ExperimentHub]{ExperimentHub}}
}
\keyword{ package }
\examples{
\donttest{
    library(oligo)
    library(hapmapsnp6)

    ## Genotype calls
    crlmmResult <- crlmmResult()
    class(crlmmResult)

    ## Raw CEL files
    cels <- celFiles()
    rawData <- read.celfiles(cels)
}
}
